## 3.2. In vitro anti-leishmanial impacts
Under in vitro and in vivo conditions, effects of various concentrations of MAA-functionalized $\mathrm{Fe}_{3}\mathrm{O}_{4}@$ bioMOFs on promastigote and amastigote forms of $L.$ major were taken into account. Under in vitro conditions, anti-leishmanial behavior against $L.$ Major promastigotes increased with both dose concentration and exposure time $(\mathtt{p}<0.05)$ . In this context, disposal time rose from 24 hours to 72 hours while the promastigotes of $L.$ . major reduced in number. As shown in Fig. 15, IC50 of the magnetic bio-MOF nanocomposites against $L.$ . major promastigotes was equal to $12.5{\pm}~0.47~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL}$ for a time period of 72 hours.
